{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>He found him in a desert land.</b> He found them faithful to Him in the land of the desert, for they accepted upon themselves His Torah and His kingdom and His yoke — which Yishma'el and Esav did not do, as it is said (Deuteronomy 33): ״וְזָרַח מִשֵּׂעִיר לָמוֹ הוֹפִיעַ מֵהַר פָּארָן״." "<b>And in the howling waste.</b> A land of drought and desolation, a place of the howling of taninim and ostriches — even there they clung after faith, and did not say to Moshe, How shall we go out into the deserts, a place of drought and desolation? As it is said (Jeremiah 2): ״לֶכְתֵּךְ אַחֲרַי בַּמִּדְבָּר״." "<b>He encompassed him.</b> There He surrounded them and encircled them with clouds, and surrounded them with standards to the four winds, and surrounded them at the foot of the mountain, which He inverted over them like a vat (cf. Sifrei)." "<b>He instructed him.</b> There, in Torah and understanding." "<b>He watched over him.</b> From snake, serpent, and scorpion, and from the nations." "<b>As the apple of his eye.</b> That is the black part of the eye, from which light goes forth. And Onkelos rendered יִמְצָאֵהוּ — 'he provided him every need in the wilderness,' as in ״מָצָא לָהֶם״ (Numbers 11), ״לֹא יִמָּצֵא לָנוּ הָהָר״ (Joshua 17)." "<b>He encompassed him.</b> 'אַשְׁרִינוּן סְחוֹר סְחוֹר לִשְׁכִנְתֵּיהּ' — the Tent of Meeting in the middle and four standards for the four directions."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:18.349348712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}